{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0623"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge nature/mammals","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/nature__mammals.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",214],["+","The best known of the echidnas, the short-beaked echidna, which Shaw had already described in 1792, is native to Australia, from the deserts to the snowfields, to Tasmania and to southern New Guinea, which sits on the same continental shelf; the other three species are the long-beaked echidnas of New Guinea. "],["=",887]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",196],["+","Der bekannteste Ameisenigel, der Kurzschnabeligel, den Shaw schon 1792 beschrieben hatte, ist in Australien heimisch, von den Wüsten bis zu den Schneefeldern, außerdem in Tasmanien und im Süden Neuguineas, das auf demselben Kontinentalschelf liegt; die übrigen drei Arten sind die Langschnabeligel Neuguineas. "],["=",835]]}]},
